title: The deputy prime minister who could not be ignored

@postal_crisis
# prose-audit: Grade A — The April 2020 crisis is staged as a live parliamentary count rather than a legal complaint: Gowin's own position, his contacts across four opposition parties and the cost of each Lewica answer are all named before the choice, and no route treats cooperation with him as a coalition.
call: poland_normalize
title: A conservative deputy prime minister asks the opposition for votes
subtitle: The postal election can only be stopped inside the United Right; Lewica decides what it will pay to help
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.postal_event_done = 1;
Q.gowin_crisis_open = 1;
const postalGovernment = Q.government_party == "lewica"
    ? "left"
    : (["independent", "other"].includes(Q.government_party)
        ? "other" : String(Q.government_party || ""));
const postalGovernmentMomentum = postalGovernment + "_poll_momentum";
if (Number.isFinite(Number(Q[postalGovernmentMomentum]))) {
    Q[postalGovernmentMomentum] =
        (Number(Q[postalGovernmentMomentum]) || 0) - 3;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 7;
}
Q.united_right_cohesion = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.united_right_cohesion) || 72) - 7
);
// Gowin's standing is the number the whole chain turns on: how much of his own
// party will still follow him when he threatens the coalition. It starts high
// because in April 2020 nobody inside Porozumienie has yet had to choose.
Q.gowin_standing = 62;
Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020 = 58;
Q.news_headline = "PiS attempts a presidential election by post";
!}

= April 2020 — The postal election

PiS intends to elect a president on 10 May by post, during an epidemic, under a
law that has not finished passing. Municipalities are told to hand over the
electoral register. The state printing works begins producing packets for a
vote that has no legal date.

The arithmetic is the story. PiS cannot pass the postal bill on its own votes,
and **Jarosław Gowin** — deputy prime minister, science minister and leader of
Porozumienie — has decided he will not supply his. He is not a democrat having
a crisis of conscience. He is a conservative who believes a rigged-looking
election will cost the right its legitimacy, and who has spent the last fortnight
proposing anything that lets him avoid choosing between his objection and his
coalition: first a postponement of about a year, then a constitutional
amendment extending **Andrzej Duda**'s term by two years with no re-election.

He is also, remarkably, talking to everyone. PSL first, then KO, then
intermediaries to Lewica, and — because the count requires it — to
Konfederacja. A sitting deputy prime minister is quietly asking the opposition
whether it can hold a line with him for one vote.

We have to answer a narrow question without pretending it is a wide one.
Helping Gowin stop the postal election is not an alliance with Gowin, and
saying so clearly is most of the work.

- @postal_tactical
- @postal_refuse
- @postal_emergency
- @postal_break
- @postal_constitutional

@postal_tactical
# prose-audit: Grade A — The narrow-objective route buys real parliamentary resistance and pays for it in progressive credibility and an opponent who now owns the outcome, with the distinction between cooperation and coalition stated in the text rather than assumed.
title: Cooperate on the count and on nothing else
subtitle: The strongest parliamentary resistance; Gowin keeps ownership of the result and our own left will ask what we bought
on-arrival: {!
Q.postal_election_stance = "Democratic legal front";
Q.gowin_channel = 34;
Q.gowin_standing += 10;
Q.postal_resistance = 46;
Q.ko_relation += 4;
Q.psl_relation += 5;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 4;
Q.judicial_legitimacy += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 4;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
Q.postal_pressure_record =
    "Lewica held technical contacts with Gowin's office on the count";
Q.news_headline =
    "A deputy prime minister and the opposition agree on one vote only";
!}

Our deputies meet his people about the count and refuse to meet them about
anything else. No joint platform, no joint press conference, no shared
statement about the epidemic or the constitution — a list of names on both
sides who will be in the chamber, and an agreement that neither of us will
claim the other has changed.

It works because it is small. It costs us because it is small: our own
progressives want to know why we are counting heads with a man who voted for
every judicial law we opposed, and the answer — that fifty-nine deputies is
fifty-nine deputies — satisfies nobody who was not already persuaded.

- @gowin_resignation

@postal_refuse
# prose-audit: Grade A — Refusal is a defensible position with a stated price: it protects the Left's record against a government minister and measurably weakens the only parliamentary count that can stop the vote.
title: Refuse to legitimise a member of the government
subtitle: Clean record, weaker resistance; Gowin has to find his majority without us
on-arrival: {!
Q.postal_election_stance = "Boycott";
Q.gowin_channel = 0;
Q.gowin_standing -= 6;
Q.postal_resistance = 22;
Q.progressive_credibility += 5;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 3;
Q.pis_relation -= 3;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.left_poll -= 0.3;
Q.postal_pressure_record =
    "Lewica refused all contact with the deputy prime minister";
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left will not negotiate with a minister of the government it opposes";
!}

We say it plainly: Gowin is a deputy prime minister in a government preparing
an unlawful election, and his objection does not convert him into an ally. If
he wants to stop this, he can stop it from inside the coalition that is doing
it.

It is the position we can still defend in three years. It also means the
resistance in the chamber is a conservative rebellion and a partial opposition,
not a majority, and the people counting for PiS know it by Thursday.

- @gowin_resignation

@postal_emergency
# prose-audit: Grade A — Demanding the constitutional instrument is the institutionally correct answer and the route says why it fails politically: the government will not declare a state of emergency precisely because the constitution would then postpone the election for it.
title: Demand a state of emergency instead
subtitle: The lawful route; the government will not take it, and refusing to bargain leaves the count where it was
on-arrival: {!
Q.postal_election_stance = "Democratic legal front";
Q.gowin_channel = 12;
Q.postal_resistance = 30;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 7;
Q.judicial_legitimacy += 6;
Q.public_trust += 4;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.president_relation -= 5;
Q.postal_pressure_record =
    "Lewica demanded a constitutional state of emergency rather than a bargain";
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left demands the constitutional instrument the government refuses to use";
!}

There is a lawful way to do this and it is written down: declare a state of
natural disaster, and Article 228 postpones the election by operation of law.
We say so every day, with lawyers, in the chamber and on every programme that
will have us.

The government will not do it, for the reason that makes our argument correct
and useless at the same time — the constitution would then take the decision
out of Kaczyński's hands. We are right in a way that changes no votes, and
Gowin, who wanted a negotiated postponement rather than a legal one, finds us
unhelpful.

- @gowin_resignation

@postal_break
# prose-audit: Grade A — The most aggressive route is available to any player but succeeds only against a leader whose instinct is to preserve both his party and the coalition; the attempt is recorded and its failure hardens Porozumienie against us for the rest of the term.
title: Try to break Porozumienie out of the United Right
subtitle: Offers Gowin a future outside PiS; he does not want one yet, and the attempt is repeated back to us
on-arrival: {!
Q.postal_election_stance = "Gowin postponement bargain";
Q.gowin_channel = 26;
Q.gowin_break_attempted = 1;
Q.postal_resistance = 38;
// He will not leave in April 2020. The offer still moves the people around him,
// which is what makes the rest of the year different.
Q.porozumienie_cohesion_2020 -= 8;
Q.gowin_standing -= 4;
Q.pis_relation -= 5;
Q.progressives_dissent += 6;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 4;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.postal_pressure_record =
    "Lewica publicly invited Porozumienie to leave the United Right";
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left invites Gowin to bring down the government he serves in";
!}

We make the offer in public, because a private one would be denied: leave the
coalition, and an opposition that despises your politics will not punish you
for the arithmetic. Take the science ministry with you if you must.

He says no, and he says it quickly. In April 2020 Jarosław Gowin still believes
he is the restraint inside the United Right rather than a man who will one day
have to leave it, and the offer of a future in opposition reads to him as a
threat. What it does instead is start an argument inside Porozumienie about
whether he was right to refuse — an argument that does not close.

- @gowin_resignation

@postal_constitutional
# prose-audit: Grade A — The deliberately costly route trades a genuine institutional principle for the fastest available stop, and the constitutional damage it accepts is named in the text rather than hidden in a number.
title: Accept a constitutional postponement of Duda's term
subtitle: The fastest way to stop the vote; we would be amending the constitution to solve PiS's problem
